assignee: repository-owner
author: codex-release-agent
estimated_minutes: 30
acceptance_criteria: "A replacement credential passes npm whoami; The validated credential is stored in the protected release environment; A release verifies npm, npx, and bunx installation"
definition_of_ready: A replacement credential can be configured through a protected channel without entering source control.
parent: searx-repo-health-2026
reviewer: repository-owner
risk: high
confidence: 100
sprint: 2026-07-release-automation
release: next
blocked_reason: Available candidate npm credentials are rejected by the registry with E401 Unauthorized.
reporter: codex-release-agent
severity: high
environment: Sanitized local authentication check against the public npm registry.
repro_steps: Load each candidate credential into NODE_AUTH_TOKEN independently and run npm whoami without logging the value.
expected_result: A replacement automation credential authenticates successfully and is stored in the protected release environment.
actual_result: Both candidate credentials failed authentication; the existing protected secret was left unchanged.
affected_version: repository configuration 2026-07-21
component: release
regression: false
customer_impact: Automated package publication cannot be proven with the supplied local credential until it is refreshed.
body: "Two locally available candidate npm tokens were tested independently on 2026-07-21. npm rejected both with E401. No token value, fragment, local path, username, host detail, or credential metadata was stored."
